summary:
  The second look at a shelved speaker does not wait its ten minutes.

history:
  Seen 2026-09-20: a Bluetooth speaker shelved as deaf at 22:10 was healthy
  at 22:14, and the shelf kept every corrector silent for the rest of the
  evening. The shelf now allows one later look per Bluetooth speaker per
  session. The bounds are the point: sweeping a deaf speaker on every check
  is where the beeping under the radio came from, and a wired member's relay
  clicks on every sweep.

target:
  package/contents/ui/SyncEngine.qml

find:
                  || !(sAt > 2) || Date.now() - sAt < 600000) continue;

replace:
                  || !(sAt > 2) || Date.now() - sAt < 0) continue;

expect:
  Killed by tst_syncengine::test_a_shelved_bluetooth_speaker_gets_one_more_look_and_only_one.
  Line-neutral.
